&lt;p&gt;You’ll act as a technical interface for customers and partners, translating mission requirements into practical solutions using AuterionOS, Skynode, and PX4. This is a hands-on role involving software development, system integration, troubleshooting, and field testing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain edge software in C/C++ and Python on Linux-based platforms such as Jetson and Skynode.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build containerized services using Docker and integrate edge systems with cloud infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement reliable communication and data pipelines using REST, gRPC, MQTT, WebSockets, and MAVLink.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage firmware flashing, vehicle configuration, sensor calibration, system bring-up, and software releases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate and troubleshoot avionics, sensors, payloads, communications, and other vehicle systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in flight testing, customer demonstrations, system validation, and field deployments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose and resolve hardware, software, networking, and Linux integration issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with hardware, firmware, cloud, production, operations, and QC teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a technical lead in customer engagements and translate mission requirements into system solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to CI/CD, testing, documentation, cybersecurity, and continuous engineering improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed customer and field requirements back into product and engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel as needed for integration, testing, and customer deployments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Software, Electrical, Robotics, Mechanical Engineering, Aviation, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of software engineering experience, with strong C/C++ and Python skills on Linux.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with embedded, edge, companion-computer, or IoT platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with PX4 or similar autopilot systems; MAVLink experience is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of networking and embedded protocols such as CAN, I2C, SPI, TCP/IP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Docker, cloud APIs, distributed systems, and CI/CD.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with UAV flight testing, avionics, flight control, and hardware/software integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting, communication, and customer-facing skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working independently in a fast-paced, hands-on environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for drones and autonomous systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;U.S. citizenship required; eligibility for Secret clearance preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
