&lt;p&gt;You will lead your team through the entire lifecycle of a customer engagement—from initial discovery and site surveys to the final hardware/software &quot;handshake&quot; in the field.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership &amp;amp; Mentorship:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead and scale a team of Solutions Engineers. You will provide technical guidance on complex integrations and foster a culture of proactive problem-solving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accountability: &lt;/strong&gt;Work directly with stakeholders throughout the company and keep the bar high for your exceptional team. You will have a close relationship with the Director of Hardware, CTO, CEO and VP of Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Field Deployment Oversight:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage the technical strategy for deploying applications in &quot;non-standard&quot; environments. This includes overseeing hardware site readiness, connectivity challenges, and environmental constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architectural Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the lead architect for high-stakes customer integrations. You will ensure that the hardware-to-software interface (API, firmware, or edge computing layers) is robust and scalable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the primary technical liaison for enterprise customers. You will translate customer business requirements into technical deployment plans that account for hardware latency, power constraints, and data throughput&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Feedback Loop Optimization:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with Product and R&amp;amp;D teams to communicate field-testing results and hardware compatibility issues, ensuring our product evolves to meet real-world edge cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hardware/Software Fluency&lt;/strong&gt;: 3+ years of experience in technical roles, with at least 3 years specifically focused on Hardware/Software Integration (e.g., IoT, robotics, industrial automation, or edge computing)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership Experience&lt;/strong&gt;: 1+ year managing a technical, customer-facing team (Solutions Architects, Field Engineers, or Sales Engineers)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Field Deployment Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;: Hands-on experience with field-deployed applications where &quot;turning it off and on again&quot; isn&#39;t always an option. Understanding of networking protocols is a major plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full-Stack Understanding&lt;/strong&gt;: While hardware-focused, you must understand the modern software stack (Cloud services, APIs, and Database management) to ensure data flows correctly from the field to the dashboard&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Crisis Management&lt;/strong&gt;: Proven ability to troubleshoot critical failures in the field under high pressure and with limited physical access to the hardware&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Authorization:&lt;/strong&gt; Must hold EU citizenship and be eligible to work in the European Union without restriction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended social security package&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellpass membership&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4003188002,"name":"Engineering","child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"offices":[{"id":4073095002,"name":"Munich, Germany","location":null,"child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":"http://app2.greenhouse.io/ai_opt_out_request/job_post/8395634002/ai_opt_out"},{"absolute_url":"https://auterion.com/company/careers-open-position/8499744002?gh_jid=8499744002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":6395210002,"location":{"name":"Arlington, Virginia"},"metadata":null,"id":8499744002,"updated_at":"2026-11-05T08:09:31-05:00","requisition_id":"250","title":"GNC Engineer ","company_name":"Auterion","first_published":"2026-04-09T04:50:49-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;As a GNC Engineer, you will be responsible for developing and sustaining the guidance, navigation, and control software that powers Auterion’s Skynode platform, built on PX4.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your primary focus will be enabling strike drone capabilities, including integration of Auterion’s software stack onto partner hardware and ensuring reliable performance in operational environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with product and field teams to improve system performance, support deployments, and rapidly troubleshoot issues observed during testing and real-world operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain guidance, navigation, and control (GNC) capabilities within PX4 and AuterionSDK, including new features, performance improvements, and automated testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve the US guidance controller for strike applications, ensuring robustness and mission effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, analyze, and review software requirements to meet customer needs, system performance targets, and quality standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement flight- and mission-critical onboard software for unmanned systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose and resolve GNC-related issues from field operations through flight log analysis, providing rapid initial assessment and driving root-cause resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with product, integration, and flight operations teams to support deployments and continuously improve system performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel to customer sites (typically 1–2 weeks at a time) to support platform integration, testing, and advanced GNC tuning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Masters degree in Aerospace Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Computer Science, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong grasp of flight dynamics and fundamentals of aerodynamics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in C/C++ (particularly on Linux based systems and memory-constrained embedded processors) and Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of PX4 or comparable autopilot technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience programming robotic applications in ROS/ROS2&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of Kalman filtering and other state estimation algorithms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills to keep a global team fully informed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on drone experience, including piloting, is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US citizenship &amp;amp; eligibility to obtain secret clearance required.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Base Salary Range: &lt;/strong&gt;$140,000 - $170,000&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited PTO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health Insurance (includes dental &amp;amp; vision)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical flex spending&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retirement Plan - 401k with company match&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4003188002,"name":"Engineering","child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"offices":[{"id":4139792002,"name":"Manassas, Virginia","location":null,"child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":"http://app2.greenhouse.io/ai_opt_out_request/job_post/8499744002/ai_opt_out"},{"absolute_url":"https://auterion.com/company/careers-open-position/8781495002?gh_jid=8781495002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":6513040002,"location":{"name":"Munich, Germany"},"metadata":null,"id":8781495002,"updated_at":"2026-10-14T09:02:16-04:00","requisition_id":null,"title":"Hardware Engineer","company_name":"Auterion","first_published":"2026-09-03T09:58:54-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;Our Munich engineering team develops advanced systems such as interceptors, launch platforms or reconnaissance drones, as well as quadcopters for military and defense applications. As a Hardware Engineer, you will own products and subsystems from proof of concept through production validation testing (PVT), combining mechatronic design, electronics integration, hands-on prototyping, and hardware validation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will collaborate with the Munich Flight Operations, System Integration, and Supply Chain teams, as well as with Zurich’s engineering team, transforming our core technologies into specialized, manufacturing-ready tactical assets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently own development of assigned products and subsystems for drone platforms and RF products from PoC through PVT, resolving evolving requirements and taking responsibility for quality, technical trade-offs, and delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design mechatronic assemblies and integrate electronics, balancing performance, weight, power, reliability, and manufacturability with input from specialist engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and iterate prototypes using 3D printing and mechanical assembly; integrate electronics, bring up hardware, and troubleshoot faults using bench measurements, soldering, and PCB rework as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and execute bench, integration, and field tests with Flight Operations and System Integration; verify hardware–firmware interaction, record measurements, investigate failures, and verify fixes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and select components, modules, materials, and suppliers against system requirements; work directly with contract manufacturers on build readiness and pilot production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver manufacturing handover packages covering CAD and PCB files, BOMs, assembly instructions, and test procedures, enabling manufacturing partners to build and verify reliable hardware consistently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years developing robotic, mechatronic, or embedded hardware, with a relevant engineering or Computer Science degree, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Depth in one discipline and practical breadth across mechanics, electronics, and firmware, demonstrated through working prototypes, debugging, and hardware validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read schematics, understand circuit design choices, and navigate PCB layouts to debug and integrate hardware; proficiency with relevant CAD tools and laboratory instruments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of C/C++ and Python to support firmware integration, driver testing, and test automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independent problem-solving, clear technical documentation, and effective collaboration in English with engineering, operations, and manufacturing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU citizenship and willingness to work primarily on-site in Munich with 20% travel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended social security package&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellpass membership&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4003188002,"name":"Engineering","child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"offices":[{"id":4073095002,"name":"Munich, Germany","location":null,"child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":"http://app2.greenhouse.io/ai_opt_out_request/job_post/8781495002/ai_opt_out"},{"absolute_url":"https://auterion.com/company/careers-open-position/8926311002?gh_jid=8926311002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":6576832002,"location":{"name":"Manassas, VA"},"metadata":null,"id":8926311002,"updated_at":"2026-11-02T10:27:05-05:00","requisition_id":null,"title":"Lead Production Technician","company_name":"Auterion","first_published":"2026-11-02T10:27:05-05:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;Overview&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Auterion, we build the future of drones and autonomous robots. Our US production team assembles and tests autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers, working to tight deadlines and uncompromising quality standards.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;As a Lead Production Technician, you are our most skilled hands on the build floor. You will assemble and test autonomous systems per specifications and schematics, set the standard for soldering and wiring workmanship, and guide fellow technicians to deliver quality units on schedule.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This role is ideal for a detail-oriented, certified technician who takes pride in clean workmanship, follows technical instructions precisely, and can coach others.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Assembly Work: Assemble autonomous systems and related components per specifications, schematics and work instructions. Help plan daily build priorities and keep production on schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Soldering and Wiring Quality: Perform and inspect soldering, wiring, harness and mechanical fitting work to certified workmanship standards. Rework or reject non-conforming work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train and Mentor Technicians: Coach assembly technicians on soldering, wiring and assembly technique. Check their work, give feedback and help maintain skills and certifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct Functional Checks and Troubleshooting: Run initial functionality checks on completed units, troubleshoot issues at the component and wiring level, and escalate complex failures to engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain Accurate Records: Document assembly progress, test results, serial numbers and configuration. Keep build records traceable and complete.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold Quality and Safety: Ensure quality standards and safety protocols are met, including ESD controls, safe handling of batteries and tools, and a clean, organized workstation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Process Improvement: Give engineering and production leadership practical feedback to improve build instructions, tooling, fixtures and yield.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage Materials and Equipment: Keep soldering stations, tools and fixtures calibrated and in good order. Track parts, flag shortages and support inventory control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support 3D Printing and Fabrication: Use 3D printing and basic CAD to produce fixtures, mounts and small parts as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Certifications&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Required: Current IPC J-STD-001 (Requirements for Soldered Electrical and Electronic Assemblies) certification, at least CIS (Certified IPC Specialist) level, or the ability to obtain it within 30 days of hire.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strongly Preferred: IPC/WHMA-A-620 (Requirements and Acceptance for Cable and Wire Harness Assemblies) certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strongly Preferred: IPC-A-610 (Acceptability of Electronic Assemblies) certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plus: IPC J-STD-001 or IPC-A-610 CIT (Trainer) credential, or NASA-STD-8739 / military soldering certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This role demands a blend of hands-on craftsmanship, technical discipline and leadership, in line with our core values: Be Bold, Own the Outcome, and Team Over Players.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated Skill: Proven hands-on through-hole and surface-mount soldering, rework and wire termination. Able to show examples of work or pass a practical soldering assessment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant Experience: Experience in electronics assembly, robotics, RC aircraft or drones, or mechanical assembly. Prior lead, trainer or mentoring experience is a plus. Experience working in an ISO9001 or AS9100 certified manufacturing facility is desired.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Documentation: Able to read and follow technical diagrams, schematics and manuals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and Fabrication Familiarity: Familiarity with 3D printing and basic CAD design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshooting: Able to troubleshoot simple electrical and mechanical issues and run basic functionality checks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attention to Detail: Consistent, accurate record-keeping and a strong quality mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reliability: Able to work a full-time, on-site Monday–Friday schedule and meet tight deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Benefits&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited PTO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health Insurance (includes dental &amp;amp; vision)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical flex spending&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retirement Plan – 401k with company match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;About Auterion&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you&#39;ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4003188002,"name":"Engineering","child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"offices":[{"id":4139792002,"name":"Manassas, Virginia","location":null,"child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":"http://app2.greenhouse.io/ai_opt_out_request/job_post/8926311002/ai_opt_out"},{"absolute_url":"https://auterion.com/company/careers-open-position/8852070002?gh_jid=8852070002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":6543587002,"location":{"name":"Munich, Germany "},"metadata":null,"id":8852070002,"updated_at":"2026-10-23T06:32:09-04:00","requisition_id":null,"title":"Manufacturing Finance Manager","company_name":"Auterion","first_published":"2026-09-28T10:29:25-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Manufacturing Finance Manager to own the operational accounting and financial management across our supply chain and procurement process - from purchase order through delivery, receipt and invoicing. The role sits within our joint venture manufacturing entity and works closely with both the JV&#39;s operations team and Auterion&#39;s central finance function. This is a hands-on, cross-functional role for someone who understands how physical goods move through a production environment and can translate that into accurate, timely financial reporting and management-ready cost visibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the procurement-to-invoice process end to end - purchase orders, delivery receipts, goods receipt checks and stock movement - ensuring proper matching and controls at each step and maintaining the document-level audit trail required under applicable accounting standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reconcile deliveries against bills of materials and purchase records, working closely with supply chain and systems teams to keep records accurate and up to date&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn delivery and receipt data into accurate, on-time invoicing and build repeatable monthly reconciliation processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and correctly account for items delivered outside standard/contracted pricing agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track actual production costs (direct materials, labor, and overhead) against contract value and budget. Surfacing variances early so operations and management can act swiftly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and reconcile WIP balances by production order; tracking physical production progress against system records, supporting accurate period-end inventory valuation and COGS recognition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the build-out of financial controls across procurement and spend, including approval workflows and spend visibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the finance counterpart to supply chain and operations teams, providing cost visibility, variance analysis, and the financial and cash-flow impact of production activity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a regular on-site presence to verify physical inventory and operations against system records&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and control operational spend against budget, including cost category visibility, variance reporting, and enforcement of non-production spend approvals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in supply chain, procurement, or operations finance - manufacturing or hardware environments strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working directly with bills of materials, purchase orders and delivery documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on cost accounting experience in a manufacturing environment: WIP tracking, standard vs. actual cost variance, inventory valuation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong reconciliation and process-control mindset; comfortable building structure where processes are still maturing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ERP ownership in a manufacturing or supply chain environment required. You build and own processes, not just use them. NetSuite experience is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communicator, comfortable working cross-functionally with supply chain, operations and finance stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;On-site presence required as this role works directly with production and receiving teams and cannot be performed remotely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in German, with a solid understanding of the German accounting and financial reporting environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended social security package&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellpass membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4099092002,"name":"Finance & Legal","child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"offices":[{"id":4073095002,"name":"Munich, Germany","location":null,"child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":"http://app2.greenhouse.io/ai_opt_out_request/job_post/8852070002/ai_opt_out"},{"absolute_url":"https://auterion.com/company/careers-open-position/8923178002?gh_jid=8923178002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":6575671002,"location":{"name":"Munich, Germany"},"metadata":null,"id":8923178002,"updated_at":"2026-10-29T06:26:24-04:00","requisition_id":"6","title":"Mission Coordinator","company_name":"Auterion","first_published":"2026-10-29T06:26:24-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Mission Coordinator to join our Mission Development team based in Munich. In this position, you will play a key role in deploying Auterion&#39;s autonomous systems and mission-critical software to active defence and public safety users. Working alongside the Mission Operations Specialist, you will help navigate fluid priorities, partial information, and evolving operational demands, bringing clarity to complex environments to keep vital initiatives with the Bundeswehr and industry partners on schedule.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Day to day, you will drive project progress with the Bundeswehr and commercial partners: tracking open action items across stakeholders, arranging live demonstrations and field evaluations, drafting proposals and presentations, and keeping engineering, supply chain, and the customer aligned.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This fast-paced, high-impact opportunity is ideal for an ambitious early-career professional seeking direct exposure to the German defence sector. Right from the start, you will work with military units, procurement bodies, and industry leaders and take charge of your own workstreams as you grow within the organisation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate joint projects with industry partners and internal teams, keeping track of open Mission Coordinatorpoints, milestones, and deliveries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organise customer demonstrations and field tests, from planning and logistics to on-site support and follow-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare offers, tender documents, and presentations for customers, partners, and government stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate Auterion&#39;s participation in trade fairs, conferences, and industry events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take end-to-end ownership of smaller workstreams and grow into greater responsibility over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in Business Administration, Economics, Political Science, International Relations, Engineering Management, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and the ability to translate complex topics into clear messaging and presentations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organised, proactive, and hands-on, with a clear focus on outcomes and comfortable with ambiguity in a fast-moving startup environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A team player, ready to step into multiple roles to ensure customer and company success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Google Workspace; experience with CRM systems is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An existing German security clearance (Ü1/Ü2) is strongly preferred; otherwise, you must be eligible and willing to obtain one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;First experience in defence, public security, or aerospace, familiarity with the German defence ecosystem around Munich.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior military service is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel within Europe (up to 20%)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent German and English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended social security package&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellpass membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4055737002,"name":"Sales & Marketing","child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"offices":[{"id":4073095002,"name":"Munich, Germany","location":null,"child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":"http://app2.greenhouse.io/ai_opt_out_request/job_post/8923178002/ai_opt_out"},{"absolute_url":"https://auterion.com/company/careers-open-position/8655231002?gh_jid=8655231002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":6456471002,"location":{"name":"Arlington, Virginia"},"metadata":null,"id":8655231002,"updated_at":"2026-11-05T08:19:23-05:00","requisition_id":"284","title":"Product Marketing Specialist","company_name":"Auterion","first_published":"2026-07-29T06:58:32-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;Auterion is seeking a Product Marketing Specialist to translate complex autonomy, robotics, and defense technology into clear, market-facing messaging, sales enablement, web content, and campaign materials.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role partners closely with product, engineering, business development, and marketing to develop technically accurate, customer-focused content for defense and global markets. The ideal candidate has experience marketing defense, aerospace, or other highly technical products and can simplify complex technologies into compelling narratives that resonate with military, government, and commercial audiences. You will play a key role in communicating what Auterion builds, why it matters, and how it delivers mission-critical capabilities in real-world environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop consistent product positioning, messaging, and use-case narratives for Auterion&#39;s autonomy and robotics solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product, engineering, and business development teams to translate technical capabilities into compelling customer-facing marketing materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create content for websites, landing pages, sales enablement, campaigns, presentations, one-pagers, events, and product launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build use-case narratives that connect product capabilities to customer needs, operational environments, and mission outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support customer-facing teams with clear sales materials, competitive positioning, and value messaging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adapt messaging for different defense audiences, geographic markets, and stages of the customer journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support product launches, announcements, demonstrations, campaigns, and field events with messaging, collateral, and web updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with design, social media, video, PR, and events teams to develop polished, high-impact marketing assets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-5 years of experience in product marketing, digital marketing, technical marketing, solutions marketing, sales enablement, or a related role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience marketing products or technologies within the defense, aerospace, national security, or government sectors is highly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience marketing complex technical products in B2B and/or B2G environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong writing, editing, and communication skills, with the ability to simplify technical concepts for a range of audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with product, engineering, sales, and business development teams to create accurate and effective marketing content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized, detail-oriented, and able to manage multiple projects simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing external agencies, designers, video production teams, or PR partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Writing or product marketing portfolio samples required.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US Citizenship required, with eligibility to obtain clearances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary Range: &lt;/strong&gt;$75,000 - 120,000&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited PTO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health Insurance (includes dental &amp;amp; vision)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical flex spending&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retirement Plan - 401k with company match&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our technology is deployed in real-world defense environments and supports missions where reliability, interoperability, and rapid iteration matter most.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":4003232002,"name":"Marketing","child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"offices":[{"id":4042467002,"name":"Arlington, Virginia","location":"Arlington, Virginia, United States","child_ids":[],"parent_id":null}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":null,"ai_opt_out_request_url":"http://app2.greenhouse.io/ai_opt_out_request/job_post/8655231002/ai_opt_out"},{"absolute_url":"https://auterion.com/company/careers-open-position/8742077002?gh_jid=8742077002","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":6495894002,"location":{"name":"Zurich"},"metadata":null,"id":8742077002,"updated_at":"2026-10-30T05:06:27-04:00","requisition_id":"310","title":"Senior Computer Vision Engineer","company_name":"Auterion","first_published":"2026-08-25T09:08:55-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Computer Vision Engineer to build and deploy perception systems that run onboard autonomous aerial platforms. This is not offline research. Our algorithms run in real time on embedded computers, in the air, in conditions we do not control.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work across the full stack of the problem: classical computer vision and deep learning, camera and sensor selection, calibration, model training and evaluation, and optimization for constrained hardware. You will take your work to the field, fly it, look at the logs, and improve it. Our platforms serve both commercial and government customers across applications including inspection, mapping, search and rescue and security.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you like hard real world problems and short feedback loops between an idea and a flight test, we want to talk with you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement and optimize onboard perception algorithms for real time detection, temporal association and state estimation of dynamic objects from a moving platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train, retrain and evaluate neural networks for detection and classification, including dataset curation, labelling strategy and evaluation methodology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize models and pipelines for embedded inference, working to explicit latency, throughput and compute budgets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain camera calibration and sensor synchronization procedures, including multi camera and multi sensor setups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Combine visual measurements with inertial and platform state data using filtering and estimation techniques for robust performance under egomotion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and run field test campaigns. Take algorithms from bench to flight, work with pilots and integrators on site, and close the loop on real captured data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build repeatable evaluation methods so that performance and accuracy are measurable across every iteration rather than judged by eye.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide input into camera, lens, sensor and compute selection, and evaluate hardware options against real performance data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take full ownership of computer vision deliverables. Disambiguate requirements, drive alignment across teams, keep stakeholders informed and see work through to the customer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and coach other engineers, and raise the bar on product quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Robotics or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands on experience deploying computer vision systems on resource constrained platforms, ideally robotic or aerial.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid grounding in classical computer vision: feature detection and matching, optical flow, camera models and calibration, multiple view geometry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience training and deploying convolutional neural networks for detection or classification, including the unglamorous parts: data collection, labelling quality, retraining loops and honest evaluation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rigor about timing and synchronization across sensors. Understanding of why timestamps, exposure timing and latency matter, and experience debugging problems that turned out to be timing problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in C++ and Python, with real experience in OpenCV.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of taking computer vision work end to end, from problem definition to something running in a real deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with field work, including travel to test sites and debugging from real world logs and video.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to navigate ambiguity and lead across teams in a fast moving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective communication and collaboration across engineering, product and external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU citizenship required.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;State estimation and sensor fusion. Kalman and extended Kalman filters, IMU integration, estimation under egomotion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with visual inertial odometry or visual SLAM, or other hard estimation work on a moving platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ROS2 or similar middleware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with embedded inference runtimes and model optimization such as quantization or pruning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with GPU or NPU accelerated pipelines on embedded SoCs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building CI or hardware in the loop infrastructure for perception regression testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in aerial platforms, PX4 or MAVLink based systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Car parking&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health and wellbeing support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and development opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;
