&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Embedded Performance Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; who is passionate about getting the most out of embedded systems — from low-level Linux tuning and hardware integration to high-performance video and data pipelines. This role is ideal for someone who enjoys working close to hardware, moving across the stack, and solving the kinds of problems where milliseconds, bandwidth, startup time, and system efficiency matter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work across the AuterionOS ecosystem on topics such as:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embedded Linux performance and system tuning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Low-latency video streaming and media pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;C/C++, Python, and Bash-based platform development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hardware integration, system profiling, and end-to-end optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaboration with experienced and driven engineers across Auterion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work within the Apps &amp;amp; Simulation team and collaborate with other development teams to build high-performance products for autonomous systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, optimize, and maintain performance-critical components within AuterionOS, Auterion’s custom embedded Linux distribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve end-to-end system behavior across compute, networking, video, and hardware interfaces, with a strong focus on latency, throughput, reliability, and resource efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze and optimize demanding workloads such as real-time telemetry, video streaming, media processing, and communication between distributed system components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate system bottlenecks across the full stack, from kernel and OS behavior to application-level code and tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineering and product teams to understand both internal and customer use cases, and translate them into robust technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Propose and implement new platform capabilities with a strong emphasis on measurable performance gains in real-world deployments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in daily stand-ups, release planning, and prioritization discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.Sc. or M.Sc. in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional experience writing object-oriented C++ and/or Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with embedded Linux systems, including cross-compilation, debugging, profiling, and performance tuning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on background in diagnosing and optimizing real-world system behavior, including CPU, memory, I/O, networking, boot time, and application latency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or optimizing low-latency video or data-streaming pipelines, ideally on embedded platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent understanding of software systems that span embedded devices, higher-level applications, and fully integrated products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong software engineering fundamentals, including system design, implementation, debugging, and testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with video codecs, GStreamer, RTP/RTSP, or hardware-accelerated media pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid experience with Debian/Ubuntu-based systems, Bash scripting, and systemd.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Docker and docker-compose in complex development and deployment environments, as well as qemu.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong debugging and performance analysis skills at both system and application level, combined with a proactive and self-directed working style.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in ROS2/DDS-style middleware and experienced with networking across multiple OSI layers, including REST APIs and performance-sensitive communication paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with system integration and interfacing sensors or peripherals, especially via USB and Ethernet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in an agile engineering environment with stand-ups, sprint planning, and shared ownership across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus: Experience with build systems such as CMake, including improving build performance in large-scale software projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
